      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "HTXRD is effective for evaluating high-temperature phase stability in high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "In situ HTXRD provides time- and temperature-resolved monitoring of oxide formation and phase transformations during heating.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A conventionally processed CrMnFeCoNi alloy with a characterized initial phase structure is a suitable starting material.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A conventionally processed AlCoCrFeNi alloy is also a suitable starting material for the proposed method.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alloy can be heated in an oxidizing environment while in situ diffraction patterns are collected.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed test can heat the alloy from room temperature to 1100 °C in air or a controlled oxygen atmosphere at a predetermined heating rate.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-temperature exposure of CrMnFeCoNi can produce nonprotective manganese oxides.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Protective spinel phases may emerge during oxidation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The underlying alloy matrix may undergo phase changes during high-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The onset and evolution of oxidation can be detected through the appearance of oxide diffraction peaks.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Matrix phase transformations can be detected from peak shifts and the appearance or disappearance of matrix diffraction peaks.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Temperature-dependent diffraction changes can be used to assess phase stability.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "HTXRD pattern evolution alone allows oxidation rates to be quantified.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The room-temperature diffraction pattern will initially remain stable before high-temperature changes occur.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Temperature-resolved HTXRD can identify the temperatures at which oxide phase transformations occur.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::rubric_card::000::8d6800c362"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "HTXRD may fail to detect newly formed phases present at very low volume fractions.",
